00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:15.461
- It's a lot hopeless.

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:16.696
You know, it's a,

00:08:16.696 --> 00:08:18.865 align:start size:88% position:13%
'cause now, I see the
map of the world, right?

00:08:18.865 --> 00:08:20.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
In North Korea, I did
not see map of the world.

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:22.969 align:start size:81% position:19%
I did not know
what was possible.

00:08:22.969 --> 00:08:24.937
Now, in the world,
I see the internet,

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:27.440 align:start size:97% position:3%
seeing all the human
history and Korea and world,

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.108
I know what's possible.

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:32.578
And America is the best chance
we've ever got as a humanity.

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:34.113
This is a humanities hope.

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:37.316
This is the best country
in human entire history.

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:39.452
And if people cannot
be happy in America

00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:43.222 align:start position:0%
and refuse to defend this
country and individual liberty,

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:46.492
I mean, there's nothing in the
world that is left to defend.

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:50.029 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, the only thing that
is left is evil dictatorships.

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:52.865
So that's why I'm so heartbroke.

00:08:52.865 --> 00:08:54.100
- So you write about this,

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.636
